statement:
Let n, m ∈ ℕ and assume (C1_{n,m}): for every F : ℝⁿ → ℝᵐ that is K-Lipschitz for some K ∈ ℝ≥0, and every ε ∈ ℝ≥0∞ with ε > 0, there is g : ℝⁿ → ℝᵐ of class C¹ (ContDiff ℝ 1) with Lⁿ({x : F(x) ≠ g(x) or DF(x) ≠ Dg(x)}) < ε. Let D ⊆ ℝⁿ be open and let h : ℝⁿ → ℝᵐ be Lipschitz on D with some constant K ∈ ℝ≥0. Then there are maps G_i : ℝⁿ → ℝᵐ and sets E_i ⊆ ℝⁿ (i ∈ ℕ) such that, for every i:
- G_i is C¹ on ℝⁿ;
- E_i is Borel (MeasurableSet) and E_i ⊆ D;
- for every u ∈ E_i, h(u) = G_i(u) and h has Fréchet derivative DG_i(u) at u (HasFDerivAt h (fderiv ℝ G_i u) u);
and Lⁿ(D \ ⋃_i E_i) = 0. Notation: ℝᵈ = Rn d = EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin d); Lⁿ = volume; DF(x) = fderiv ℝ F x, which is 0 where F is not differentiable.
